A table whose name has spaces goes on purpose: the step names it in double
quotes, as SQL does (and as the refusal wrote it: quoted-name-refused).

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE "dish of the day" (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO "dish of the day" VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
DROP TABLE "dish of the day";

